{"description":"Signs with --key (or $COMMONS_KEY) and commits through the store's journal: the blob and its statements land together or not at all. A draft is never stored unsigned. Your log's next seq and prev come from the statements this store holds; a FORK in your log is refused until you name --prev. --intended-for runs the named edition's rules first and refuses on fail. With availability withheld and content under 64 bytes it warns that short content may be enumerable against its hash (a heuristic; include a nonce) and proceeds; the warning is not recorded. A rotate_key draft is signed as written: none of `commons rotate`'s checks run (successor, key events already held, merged tips), so the way out after a compromise stays open; it warns and proceeds. With --as <identity> --grant <id> the statement acts for a fixed-root identity (rc/2, the actor in the signed envelope): it is refused, nothing signed, unless the identity evaluator over the statements this store holds plus this line reads the act eligible (exit 2 when it is denied, naming why; exit 3 when it cannot decide, e.g. the grant or the identity is not held). A collection's genesis (a draft) may name typed controllers ({key: K} and/or {identity: I}): it is then signed rc/2 (body marker {}, no actor) from a bare key, and refused with nothing signed unless it reads valid (sorted and duplicate-free, a rule its controllers can satisfy). Controllers that are all plain keys stay rc/1. A bare key's edition (or withdraw_approval) of a resource whose genesis is rc/2 is written rc/2, marker only, so it shares the edition id with an identity's approval of the same body; the genesis must be held (exit 3 otherwise), and an edition of a resource whose genesis is rc/1 stays rc/1. An edition naming an identity controller is refused (KNOWN-LIMITS L-21), and an act for an identity on an edition (--as) needs a grant carrying `edition` for a resource that already exists. A holds is written beside an authored or observed whose bytes this store keeps (--no-holds withholds it); it stays your key's own (rc/1): your key holds the bytes. External signing (identity profile §8): --prepare <file> --signer <key> writes an external-signing package and appends nothing; sign its PAE bytes with the key elsewhere, then --complete <file> --signature <file|-> verifies the signature over the recomputed bytes, runs every check again, and commits only when your log has not moved since (else stale-prepare, exit 1). Only an act (--as) is prepared; an authored act needs --no-holds, and its eligibility is read at --complete.","options":[{"option":"--key","summary":"the signing key file (else $COMMONS_KEY); there is no default"},{"option":"--prev","summary":"the line of your log to extend; needed when your log has a FORK, and makes a fork when it is not a tip"},{"option":"--ts","summary":"the signer-declared time (RFC 3339 UTC); default now; more than 300 s ahead is refused"},{"option":"--dry-run","summary":"print what would be signed and committed, sign nothing, write nothing"},{"option":"--draft","summary":"a JSON draft {\"kind\":…,\"body\":{…}}; the tool fills signer, seq, prev, ts and sig"},{"option":"--kind","summary":"authored, holds, describes or retracts (without --draft)"},{"option":"--content","summary":"the bytes the statement is about; installed in the store with the statements"},{"option":"--media-type","summary":"content.media_type"},{"option":"--type","summary":"authored type (default dataset)"},{"option":"--provenance","summary":"authored provenance object {workflow, inputs[, environment]}"},{"option":"--no-holds","summary":"authored or observed only: keep the bytes in the store but write no holds (a withheld artifact)"},{"option":"--about","summary":"describes: the blob or statement described"},{"option":"--note","summary":"describes: the note"},{"option":"--of","summary":"retracts: the statement retracted"},{"option":"--reason","summary":"retracts: the reason"},{"option":"--as","summary":"act for a fixed-root identity (its inception id): the statement is written rc/2 with x_actor_v1 {identity, grant}; needs --grant"},{"option":"--grant","summary":"with --as: the grant (its statement id) your key acts under"},{"option":"--amends","summary":"with --as, authored or observed only: the identity's earlier claims this one amends (identity profile §5)"},{"option":"--attribution","summary":"authored disclosure attribution"},{"option":"--availability","summary":"authored disclosure availability"},{"option":"--comparator","summary":"authored disclosure comparator"},{"option":"--description","summary":"authored disclosure description"},{"option":"--extends","summary":"authored disclosure extends"},{"option":"--fulfills","summary":"authored disclosure fulfills"},{"option":"--intended-for","summary":"run the edition's rules on the bytes before they are pinned (your own policy, chosen by naming the edition); fail refuses, ok or unchecked is recorded"},{"option":"--licence","summary":"authored disclosure licence"},{"option":"--licence-texts","summary":"authored disclosure licence_texts"},{"option":"--pre-registration","summary":"authored disclosure pre_registration"},{"option":"--replication","summary":"authored disclosure replication"},{"option":"--sampling","summary":"authored disclosure sampling"},{"option":"--shelf-life-days","summary":"authored disclosure shelf_life_days"},{"option":"--supersedes","summary":"authored disclosure supersedes"},{"option":"--prepare","summary":"do not sign: write an external-signing package (rc-signing-package/1) to this new file: the unsigned statement, the exact bytes to sign (PAE, base64), the signer, the proposed id, your log's head and a summary; needs --signer, takes no --key, appends nothing; an existing file is never overwritten"},{"option":"--signer","summary":"with --prepare: the public form of the key that will sign (ed25519:<64 hex> or 0x<40 hex>); the algorithm follows from the form"},{"option":"--complete","summary":"commit a package written by --prepare, with --signature: the bytes signed are recomputed from the package, the signature verified, every check of direct signing run again; refused, nothing appended, when your log moved since the package was prepared (stale-prepare)"},{"option":"--signature","summary":"with --complete: the signature over the package's PAE bytes in the statement encoding (ed25519: 128 lowercase hex; eip191-secp256k1: 0x + 130 lowercase hex); - reads standard input"}],"summary":"sign and commit a statement (authored with its bytes, holds, describes, retracts, or a draft)","usage":"commons publish [--key <file>] [--prev <id>] [--ts <time>] [--dry-run] [--draft <file>] [--kind <kind>] [--content <file>] [--media-type <type>] [--type <type>] [--provenance <json>] [--no-holds] [--about <digest|id>] [--note <text>] [--of <id>] [--reason <text>] [--as <identity>] [--grant <id>] [--amends <id[,id…]>] [--attribution <text>] [--availability <json>] [--comparator <digest>] [--description <text>] [--extends <digest>] [--fulfills <json>] [--intended-for <resource/edition>] [--licence <text>] [--licence-texts <json>] [--pre-registration <text>] [--replication <text>] [--sampling <json>] [--shelf-life-days <integer>] [--supersedes <digest>] [--prepare <file>] [--signer <key>] [--complete <file>] [--signature <file|->] [--json]"}
